+## Open bounded learnability finding: overlap precedence
+
+Source SHA-256: `d8bbc51697a0c549a159bec7ff97c49f494c3e445280106e377d02d59cd1ae28`.
+The generator permits overlapping anomaly paint regions. With default generation,
+seed `2`, samples `0,1,2` as visible demonstrations and sample `3` as query, the
+canonical rule and a concrete rival agree on every demonstration but disagree on
+two query cells. The rival only reverses anomaly processing order: earlier
+row-major anomalies win overlaps instead of later anomalies. No demonstration
+in this witness contains a conflicting overlap, so the required precedence is
+not identified by its visible labels.
+
+Protected Racket executed both exact programs on all four inputs (eight
+evaluations); all four generated inputs pass the selected generator's
+`self_check`. The bounded structural search stopped after 12 draws across seeds
+`0..2`. This is one named-rival counterexample, not a broad safety or universal
+learnability verdict. Production source and approval state were not changed.
+
+Reproduce from the packet root:
+`WORK/.venv/bin/python review.py run python3 ../checks/a1ece4864521/probe.py`.
+Retained evidence: `WORK/checks/a1ece4864521/` (`probe.py`, `result.json`,
+`challenge.public.json`, `labels.private.json`, `canonical.rkt`,
+`rival_reverse_precedence.rkt`, `assets_manifest.json`). The result binds source,
+program and runtime hashes; private labels contain exact inputs/outputs and
+per-grid hashes. There was no retained `evidence/review_index.json` at review.
+
+Potential repair choices for an owner: ensure demonstrations expose overlap
+precedence whenever a query needs it, or disallow conflicting overlaps. These
+are proposals only; no repair was attempted in this bounded peer review.
